# From the copy that was bootstrap/examples/assumed-need-incoherent.moss (removed; its
# oracle verdicts are the old Rocq oracle's, historical):
# AssumesComplete (AUDIT-CHANGES #57; D20; criteria section 6, fidelity).
# Each assumed item's requirements are in force and its own needs provided.
# Here: f needs h at T = U; g assumes h at T = T, so f's need is provided at another instantiation (Satisfies' coherence clause). tests/wasi/assumed_need_coherent.moss is the control.
# Audit before: accepts. Audit now: rejects (argued from the rules, not run).
# Oracle (moss_m2): rejects ("calling `f` needs `h` at another instantiation ... (D62)").
# Native (ob-family moss, seed 1h1710x0): accepts (native does not check an assumed item's needs' instantiations).
type T;
type U;
assume T { fn h(); }
context H = U, h[T = U];
assume H { fn f(); }
# AUDIT-CHANGES #57 (D62): `f` needs `h` at `T = U`, and the `h` assumed
# beside it is at `T = T`, though `g` never calls `f`.
assume T, U, h, f { fn g() {} }
fn main() {}
